  "details": "Please revert the change with remote users' camera shutter sounds being controlled by \"World\" volume instead of \"UI\" volume. At least, this shouldn't be done without providing an option to mute or control remote camera shutter sounds separately\n\nThere are different reasons why users might disable the camera sound, but mine is that it's really disruptive in large event instances where people are taking a lot of photos, and all you hear is *shutter**shutter**shutter*. Muting UI sounds before was more like an ok workaround since UI sounds aren't essential. But now that it's tied to world volume, it's pretty much impractical to turn off, especially in music focused event worlds\n\nSee also this highly voted past canny: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/be-quieter-the-camera-shutter-sound",
